iv><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>account + what’s happening from <b>Signal Console</b></li><li>who to call (the person + their role)</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>on a booked meeting → <b>creates a Deal</b> (into Deal Workspace)</li><li>call outcomes → <b>Dashboard</b> · <b>Deal Workspace</b> · <b>Readiness</b> · <b>sales handoff documentation</b></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Language — plain, mid-sales-legible</div><h2>The user is the seller</h2><div data-copy-context="deprecated-example" class="sd">Banned on the face: thread · loom · pull · pressure · proof · say-next · call memory · “the move.” The user is the <b>seller</b> (or <i>you</i>), never “rep.”</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>The deal-creation on a booked meeting</li><li>The prep-then-capture shape</li><li>The live consequence of a real call</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never a script library</li><li>Never a during-call clicker</li><li>Not a live-call console</li><li>Not a dialer</li></ul></div></div></div>
