s="sec"><div class="sn">3 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Seven authored sections</b></td><td>Prose that reads like a document a sharp operator wrote for their replacement — not aggregated bullet lists.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Per-section status</b></td><td>ready / partial / empty — shown honestly, thin parts not hidden.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The per-section cross-room read</b></td><td>The “one thing to notice” — the read no single room can surface alone.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The open-book reader</b></td><td>A two-pane bound reader: contents + readiness on the left plate, one authored part in full reading serif (Newsreader) on the right page.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Section-readiness count</b></td><td>A recessive “N of 7 parts ready” segment bar — never the hero.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The share-link mechanic</b></td><td>Read-mode workspace access for an external email — the one durable move.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The ceremony hook</b></td><td>Fires the set-piece on the first upward Readiness transition into Inheritable-with-guardrails.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · The ceremony moment</div><h2>The kit becomes real</h2><div class="sd">When Readiness transitions UP from <b>Building → Inheritable with guardrails</b> for the first time in a workspace, fire a set-piece (not a toast): an animated reveal — the verdict change, the kit count moving (e.g. 2/7 → 4/7), a serif headline (“the kit just became real”), and a one-time CTA to share the workspace read-mode. Once per workspace per upward transition; downward transitions are silent.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class=