ives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Seven authored sections</b></td><td>Evidence-based prose that explains observed patterns and their limitations to another seller.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Per-section status</b></td><td>ready / partial / empty, with incomplete sections and evidence limits visible.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The per-section cross-workspace assessment</b></td><td>The “one thing to notice” — an assessment combining evidence from multiple workspaces.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The open-book reader</b></td><td>A two-pane bound reader: contents + readiness on the left plate, one authored part in full reading serif (Newsreader) on the right page.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Section-readiness count</b></td><td>A recessive “N of 7 parts ready” segment bar — never the hero.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The share-link mechanic</b></td><td>Read-mode workspace access for an external email — the persistent sharing control.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The ceremony hook</b></td><td>Triggers the existing visual transition on the first upward Readiness transition into Runnable with founder support.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · The ceremony moment</div><h2>Sales handoff readiness improves</h2><div class="sd">When Readiness transitions UP from <b>Partially documented → Runnable with founder support</b> for the first time in a workspace, show the existing visual transition (not a toast): an animated reveal — the verdict change, the kit count moving (e.g. 2/7 → 4/7), a serif headline (“Sales handoff documentation is ready to review”), and a one-time CTA to share the workspace read-mode. Once per workspace per upward transition; downward transitions are silent.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li><b>every cloud-synced room</b> — ICP Studio (§1) · Deal Workspace closed deals (§1/4/5/6) · Outbound + LinkedIn + Cold Call (§2) · Discovery segment-jump data (§3) · Call in a Favor (§4) · Future Autopsy (§5) · Quota Workback + Deal pipeline (§7)</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>section-readiness count into the <b>Dashboard</b> + <b>Readiness</b> anchor (the “5/7 ready” stat)</li><li>section-readiness count drives the Readiness “Documented and repeatable” gate (≥ 5/7)</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>Specific operator recommendations supported by recorded evidence</li><li>The cross-room “one thing to notice” reads</li><li>The ceremony moment</li><li>Section 7’s prescriptive cadence is the operating rhythm, not metrics</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never an export of room data</li><li>Never a bullet-list aggregator (the legacy room was that; the rebuild explicitly is not)</li><li>Never a dashboard of section-cards</li><li>Never just a scoreboard</li></ul></div></div></div>
