-  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Onboarding · Threshold · capability map</div><h1>Do the hard work once. The system plays it back forever.</h1><div class="fam">Threshold (entry) · the heavy-seeding flow · governed by ADR-019 + canon §12</div><p>Seed the workspace deep enough that the app “rises up to greet” the operator — every room already live, the Dashboard already handing back a real first move — as a side effect of the operator doing the judgment-heavy work only they can do. Not a low-friction form: a <b>deliberate seeding</b> that asks for the heavy, only-in-your-head thinking and frames it as capitalizing an asset that pays a dividend every morning after.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.3 + the heavy-seeding doctrine (Part III §12) + ADR-019 (approved, build in progress). Settled design: onboarding-seeding-flow-2026-07-07.html (+ 3 companion validated prototypes).</div></div>
-  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Seed the living rooms (ICP Studio, Signal Console, Deal Workspace, Quota Workback) deep enough that the workspace is <b>already operational</b> when the operator lands on Welcome. The doctrine’s line: <b>we never apologize for the work — we make it obviously worth it, in real time, and tell the operator they’re doing the thing no one else does.</b> They bring irreducible judgment; the app brings enrichment.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The seven-step arc</div><h2>The settled seeding flow</h2><div class="sd">A fixed, ordered flow. The heavy middle (live deals) is the judgment no automation can supply; everything the app can enrich, it enriches.</div><table><tr><th style="width:26px">#</th><th style="width:180px">Step</th><th>What it asks / does</th></tr><tr><td><span class="n">1</span></td><td><b>Doorway</b></td><td>Leads with the honesty — “this asks real work of you, here’s the deal.” The honest pitch, not an apology.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">2</span></td><td><b>ICP</b></td><td>Interview-style — the app pushes back on a vague answer until it’s a target it can hunt.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">3</span></td><td><b>Accounts</b></td><td>Takes <b>names only</b> (breadth is cheap) and enriches them — triggers, firmographics, heat. They visibly rise up.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">4</span></td><td><b>Wake-up</b></td><td>The seed→alive reveal — the system reads the named accounts back, enriched.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">5</span></td><td><b>Live deals</b></td><td>The heavy middle — the operator fills the judgment only they hold (champion, who signs, where it’s stuck); the company came enriched. Deals wake toward the floor.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">6</span></td><td><b>Quota</b></td><td>The number set — seeds Quota Workback + the outbound seed.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">7</span></td><td><b>Landing</b></td><td>The system reads everything it was given and hands back the one move that needs the operator first → Welcome.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · The tier model</div><h2>Gate the load-bearing, invite the rest</h2><div class="sd">Heavy-seeding doctrine #6. The deal-level judgment is the hard floor — the thing that stops Antaeus being a prettier CRM.</div><table><tr><th style="width:140px">Tier</th><th>What</th><th>Rule</th></tr><tr><td><b>Required</b></td><td>ICP + the account list + <b>≥10 live deals</b></td><td>Gated. Fewer than ten is allowed but the app says plainly it stays thin.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Invited</b></td><td>pilot evidence · advisors · win/loss history</td><td>Post-landing, payoff-anchored prompts gathered over days — never walled.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The doorway</b></td><td>The honest pitch — frames the friction as the sign they’re doing the rare thing.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The interview-style ICP sharpener</b></td><td>Pushes back on a vague answer until the ICP is a target the system can hunt.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Name-only account capture → enrichment</b></td><td>Operator gives names; the app returns triggers / firmographics / heat.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The live-deal judgment cards</b></td><td>champion / who signs / where it’s stuck / budget-timeline — the only-they-know judgment; the company arrives enriched.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The ≥10-deal floor</b></td><td>The hard judgment floor, with an honest thin-edge when the operator has fewer.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The quota set</b></td><td>The number, worked into the daily habit downstream.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The landing hand-off</b></td><td>The system reads everything and hands back the one move.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The persistent evidence margin</b></td><td>A recessive, blue <b>“why we ask”</b> note on every ask that opens to a real, citable source — never assertion.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="sd">Onboarding does not store to a separate “completion” record — its output <b>becomes</b> the live rooms.</div><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>new-user context (company, role, product category)</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li><span class="mono">gtmos_icp_analytics</span> — the sharpened ICP (→ ICP Studio)</li><li><span class="mono">gtmos_sc_v4</span> + <span class="mono">gtmos_signal_room_health</span> — accounts (→ Signal Console)</li><li><span class="mono">gtmos_deal_workspaces</span> — the live deals (→ Deal Workspace)</li><li><span class="mono">gtmos_qw_inputs</span> + <span class="mono">gtmos_outbound_seed</span> — quota (→ Quota Workback)</li><li><span class="mono">gtmos_activation_context</span> + <span class="mono">gtmos_onboarding</span> — completion; all cloud-mirrored via ADR-007. Hands off to <b>Welcome</b>.</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>Heavy-seeding — never re-soften into a low-friction form that apologizes for the work</li><li>Onboarding output <b>becoming</b> the live rooms (never a separate “completion” screen)</li><li>The ≥10-deal judgment floor</li><li>The citable evidence margin</li><li>“They bring judgment, the app brings depth”</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Not a low-friction sign-up form</li><li>Not a CRM data-entry grid</li><li>Not a wizard that hides the work</li><li>Not a backstage record the operator never returns to</li></ul></div></div></div>
