ees the banned word.</div><table data-copy-context="deprecated-example"><tr><th style="width:260px">Banned on the face</th><th>Say instead</th></tr><tr><td>proof · cast · mold · forge/foundry · ingot · heat/heat-ledger · kill rule · readout</td><td>the pilot · the results · the evidence</td></tr><tr><td>the quality band</td><td>ready / almost ready / more detail required</td></tr><tr><td>the mold grid</td><td>the parts of the pilot</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>The guide (never a scorecard or checklist)</li><li>Adoption as the success meter (never the outcome number alone)</li><li>The people / multi-threading layer (right-sized, never “get everyone”)</li><li>The who’s-missing prompt</li><li>The feel-of-ease (never a wall of fields)</li><li>The Share kit + Mutual pilot plan</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never a scorecard</li><li>Never a checklist</li><li>Never a wall of fields</li><li>Not a metrics dashboard</li></ul></div></div></div>
