-  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Territory Architect · Decision Bench · capability map</div><h1>The ICP, carved into a territory you actually own.</h1><div class="fam">Decision Bench (strategic shaping) · settled 2026-07-04 (axis-morphing floor)</div><p>Turn the ICP into a tiered territory with focuses, approaches, and a hard <b>300-account ceiling</b> that forces strategic ownership. The territory is a map of focused groups of buyers, not a list. A focus is a named <b>division</b> of the market, carved on whatever axis fits the motion — and the axes blend.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.5 (carve-axis malleability + why-you/why-now charter, 2026-07-03) + shipped src/territory-architect. Settled design: territory-architect-axis-morph-2026-07-04.html.</div></div>
-  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Carve the ICP into divisions the seller can actually own. The carve axis is a <b>variable, not a constant</b> — the room stays malleable from a scorch-the-earth pre-seed (one coarse division) to an organized Series B (a geo × vertical grid). The 300-cap + swap make each account consequential; tiers are a resource-allocation commitment, not a ranking.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The carve axes</div><h2>How a division is cut — blendable</h2><div class="sd">However a division is carved, the same machinery sits on top: a tier, a share of the 300-cap, an approach, and a charter. The room <b>morphs its register</b> to the axis.</div><table><tr><th style="width:150px">Axis</th><th>Reads like</th></tr><tr><td><b>Geography</b></td><td>cartographic</td></tr><tr><td><b>Industry / vertical</b></td><td>an industry board</td></tr><tr><td><b>Segment</b> (size / ACV / stage)</td><td>a segment grid</td></tr><tr><td><b>Named accounts</b></td><td>a named list</td></tr><tr><td><b>Trigger / behavior</b></td><td>pressure charters</td></tr><tr><td><b>Blended</b> (e.g. West Coast × FinTech × Series B+)</td><td>a coverage funnel keeping the blend legible</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · The charter rule</div><h2>Every division states why</h2><div class="sd">The charter adapts its ask to the axis so the operator never reads the rule.</div><table><tr><th style="width:150px">Field</th><th>Rule</th></tr><tr><td><b>Why-you</b> (why we’re the right team)</td><td><b>required</b> — every division, every axis</td></tr><tr><td><b>Why-now</b> (what pressure is on them)</td><td><b>required</b> for trigger carves · optional-but-encouraged for structural carves</td></tr><tr><td><b>Signals</b></td><td>must be <b>observable</b> (a fresh raise, a new exec, a hiring surge) — never a trigger no one can detect</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Sales-cycle calibration</b></td><td>Tunes the territory to the motion’s cycle length.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The carve axis</b></td><td>geo / vertical / segment / named / trigger — blendable; sets the room’s register.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Focuses / divisions</b></td><td>The named cuts of the market.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Per-division charter</b></td><td>why-you (required) · why-now (conditional on axis).</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Approaches + the approach ledger</b></td><td>How each division gets worked, tracked.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Tiers</b></td><td>A resource-allocation commitment, not a ranking.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Focus-to-account tagging</b></td><td>Which accounts belong to which division.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The 300-cap allocation</b></td><td>count-vs-target per tier + a swap mechanic — each account is consequential.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li><b>ICP Studio</b> (the sharpened target)</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>tier + focus into <b>Prospecting Desk</b></li><li>tier + focus into <b>Signal Console</b></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>The strategic tier logic</li><li>The act of naming a division</li><li>Axis-malleability (never hardcode one carve)</li><li>The why-you charter on every division</li><li>Divisions standing on detectable signals</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never a contact-list builder</li><li>Not a static map</li><li>Not a ranked leaderboard of accounts</li><li>Not a single-axis (geo-only) territory tool</li></ul></div></div></div>
