 <div class="map"><h2>4. What this room is for and how it works</h2><p>The room's capability map: its purpose, every part and what it does, what flows in from and out to other rooms, and what it must never become.</p><div class="wrap">
-  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Briefing · Intelligence Surface · capability map</div><h1>What the system saw — inside your work and out in the market.</h1><div class="fam">Intelligence Surface (new family, closest neighbor System Ledger) · named premium asset · ADR-006</div><p>The daily check-in for what the system saw — both inside the operator’s own work (the <b>Workspace</b> stream) and in the market the operator is selling into (the <b>World</b> stream). Written like a peer telling them what they see. Not “what to act on next” (the Dashboard’s job) and not “which accounts are on the radar” (Signal Console’s job).</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.21 + ADR-006 + ADR-009 + ADR-014 + the 13 promoted specs (deliverables/specs/briefing). Settled design: briefing-vivid-2026-07-04.html.</div></div>
-  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Be the daily check-in for what the system saw. The operator’s stated preferences (watchlist, ICP, competitive set) are treated as <b>hypotheses under continuous evaluation</b>, not fixed truths to serve. A responsive product accepts them as given; the Briefing tests them continuously and tells the operator when the evidence isn’t supporting the hypothesis.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The two streams</div><h2>One room, one toggle</h2><div class="sd">The Workspace / World toggle is the room’s organizing axis, not optional decoration. Default is Workspace.</div><table><tr><th style="width:150px">Stream</th><th>Subject</th><th>Cadence · cost</th></tr><tr><td><b>Workspace</b></td><td>the operator’s own deals / signals / pilots (the ADR-009 ledger)</td><td>daily-fresh · SQL heartbeat generators</td></tr><tr><td><b>World</b></td><td>the market — Recipe-Layer Patterns + Contrarian + Periphery</td><td>weekly synthesis · full Recipe Layer</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · The provocative posture</div><h2>Three obligations the operator did not ask for</h2><div class="sd">The Briefing is provocative, not responsive — it serves stated preferences AND takes on three additional obligations.</div><table><tr><th style="width:150px">Obligation</th><th>What it means</th></tr><tr><td><b>Coverage</b></td><td>surface entities the operator hasn’t named but the data says they should watch (Periphery)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Framing</b></td><td>challenge interpretations the operator has committed to when the evidence contradicts them (Contrarian)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Defensibility</b></td><td>preserve enough state at every synthesis to reconstruct what the system said, on what basis, months later (Audit Envelopes)</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives (Recipe Layer)</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Pattern</b></td><td>a synthesized read: claim + evidence + confidence + audit envelope.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>ContrarianPattern</b></td><td>a challenge to a stated assumption.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Periphery Candidate</b></td><td>an off-watchlist entity the data says should be on it.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Watchlist Trigger</b></td><td>an operator-issued standing order — five types: single_event / aggregation / threshold / adjacency / silence.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Deal-Watch Alert</b></td><td>an item that intersects an active deal.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Audit Envelope</b></td><td>an immutable JSON capture of cluster + hydrated context + LLM call chain + cost at every synthesis.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Voice Document</b></td><td>banned vocab + 5 exemplars + structural rules + hedging rules — the editorial brain driving every quality gate.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Behavioral Feedback</b></td><td>operator-marked Used / Already-knew / Noise that tunes weights.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · The pipeline</div><h2>How a Pattern is made</h2><div class="sd">Wrapped end-to-end by the Audit Envelope subsystem; watched by the Evaluation Harness (pre-merge gates + production sampling with retroactive scoring).</div><ul class="plain"><li>Context Hydration → Ingest → Filter → Enrich → Periphery Detection → Cluster → <b>Synthesize</b> (Draft → Critique → Revise → Quality Gate) → Contrarian Synthesis → Score → Surface → Briefing Compose</li><li><b>Cost discipline:</b> per-user weekly LLM ceiling + separate harness ceiling. Warning at 80%, throttle at 100% (Sonnet substitution + tighter relevance), pause at 150%. Cost telemetry on the footer of every briefing.</li></ul></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="sd">The Briefing is the <b>intelligence surface</b> that reads from the <b>Signal Console</b> substrate (accounts + signals + heat in Postgres). It never writes to those tables.</div><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>every room’s <span class="mono">getState()</span> contract (ICP · Discovery · Outbound · Asset Builder · Deal Workspace · Watchlist Triggers · Voice Document · Behavioral Feedback)</li><li>the <b>Signal Console</b> substrate’s accounts + signals</li><li>external sources per the Intelligence Coverage Audit</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li><span class="mono">recommended_moves[].destination</span> <b>drafts</b> into Discovery Studio · Asset Builder · Outbound · Deal Workspace</li><li>the Briefing never writes directly — it produces drafts the operator reviews and saves to the destination</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">7 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>The provocative obligations (Coverage, Framing, Defensibility)</li><li>The Voice Document’s editorial discipline</li><li>The audit envelope’s immutability</li><li>The Workspace / World toggle as the organizing axis</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never a feed</li><li>Never an inbox</li><li>Never a notification center</li><li>Not the Dashboard (“what to act on”) or Signal Console (“who’s on the radar”)</li></ul></div></div></div>
