 <div class="map"><h2>4. What this room is for and how it works</h2><p>The room's capability map: its purpose, every part and what it does, what flows in from and out to other rooms, and what it must never become.</p><div class="wrap">
-  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Future Autopsy · Diagnosis Table · capability map</div><h1>Pre-mortem the deal before it dies.</h1><div class="fam">Diagnosis Table (intervention) · named premium asset · settled 2026-07-04 (the countdown)</div><p>Pre-mortem the deal before it dies; show the causal pattern and the corrective route. The deal is <b>pinned as evidence</b> on a forensic light-table. The analysis surfaces the causal pattern (e.g. <i>pressure before clarity</i>), the intervention options, and a command row. The positive example the other Diagnosis Table rooms should borrow from.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.14 + the autopsy generator + deal-health subset (shipped src/future-autopsy). Settled design: future-autopsy-countdown-2026-07-04.html (the decay line).</div></div>
-  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Diagnose failure <b>before</b> it happens. Forensic light-table posture: each at-risk deal is pinned as a case, its causal pattern named, its corrective route made obvious. Never soften into “risk review” — this is consequential route correction, not commentary.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The analysis</div><h2>What each pinned case shows</h2><table><tr><th style="width:180px">Element</th><th>What it is</th></tr><tr><td><b>The causal pattern</b></td><td>the named failure shape — e.g. “pressure before clarity”</td></tr><tr><td><b>Intervention options</b></td><td>change the 3× deal truth · test the risk-fix lens · rebuild the agenda</td></tr><tr><td><b>The horizon tag</b></td><td>how many days out the death is</td></tr><tr><td><b>The command row</b></td><td>Run selected · Urgent autopsy deal · Copy brief</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The pinned-case ledger</b></td><td>The live set of at-risk deals pinned as evidence — count is dynamic, never hardcoded.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The horizon tag</b></td><td>Days-out until the deal dies if nothing changes.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The causal-pattern narrative</b></td><td>The named failure pattern behind the case.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The intervention options</b></td><td>The concrete corrective lenses to run.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The command row</b></td><td>Run selected · Urgent autopsy deal · Copy brief.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The route rack</b></td><td>Back to Deal Workspace / Discovery Studio / Pilot Desk — the corrective destinations.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>deals with pressure/stage truth from <b>Deal Workspace</b></li><li>unresolved gaps from <b>Discovery Studio</b></li><li>pilot state from <b>Pilot Desk</b></li><li>(loss-pattern feedback from <b>Getting to Signed</b> — was it lost in procurement, before anyone argued terms?)</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>reroute logic into <b>Deal Workspace</b> · <b>Discovery Studio</b> · <b>Pilot Desk</b></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>Failure-pattern diagnosis</li><li>Consequential route correction</li><li>Strategic severity</li><li>The pinned-as-evidence posture (count dynamic, never hardcoded)</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never soften into “risk review”</li><li>Not a status dashboard</li><li>Not a boxed warning-board</li><li>Not abstract diagnosis without a corrective move</li></ul></div></div></div>
+<div class="callout blue"><div class="ct">Language and capability review · 2026-11-02</div><div class="cb">Use the current source and docs/language-remediation-2026 for implementation. Earlier design references below preserve history; they do not authorize deprecated customer language or capabilities that the source does not implement. Keep stable internal identifiers separate from display wording. Distinguish evidence, assessment, forecast, and recommendation.</div></div>
+  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Future Autopsy · deal-risk review · capability map</div><h1>Review deal-loss risk and corrective actions.</h1><div class="fam">deal-risk review (intervention) · named premium asset · settled 2026-07-04 (the countdown)</div><p>Future Autopsy uses recorded deal conditions to assess risk and recommend corrective actions. Its scenario is an assessment, not a recorded loss or a causal explanation of an event that has not happened.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.14 + the autopsy generator + deal-health subset (shipped src/future-autopsy). Settled design: future-autopsy-countdown-2026-07-04.html (the decay line).</div></div>
+  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Show the recorded conditions, risk assessment, evidence, corrective actions, and when to consider closing the opportunity. The heuristic review window is not a predicted loss date. Preserve the product name, visual identity, routing, and task state.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The analysis</div><h2>What each pinned case shows</h2><table><tr><th style="width:180px">Element</th><th>What it is</th></tr><tr><td><b>The risk-factor assessment</b></td><td>the recorded conditions associated with risk and their supporting evidence</td></tr><tr><td><b>Intervention options</b></td><td>change the 3× deal truth · test the risk-fix lens · rebuild the agenda</td></tr><tr><td><b>The horizon tag</b></td><td>the heuristic interval for reviewing the deal again</td></tr><tr><td><b>The command row</b></td><td>Run selected · Urgent autopsy deal · Copy brief</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The pinned-case ledger</b></td><td>The live set of at-risk deals pinned as evidence — count is dynamic, never hardcoded.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The horizon tag</b></td><td>Heuristic review interval; it does not predict a loss date.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The risk-factor narrative</b></td><td>An assessment of the recorded risk factors and their limitations.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The intervention options</b></td><td>The concrete corrective lenses to run.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The command row</b></td><td>Run selected · Urgent autopsy deal · Copy brief.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The route rack</b></td><td>Back to Deal Workspace / Discovery Studio / Pilot Desk — the corrective destinations.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>recorded deal stage and risk factors from <b>Deal Workspace</b></li><li>unresolved gaps from <b>Discovery Studio</b></li><li>pilot state from <b>Pilot Desk</b></li><li>(loss-pattern feedback from <b>Getting to Signed</b> — was it lost in procurement, before anyone argued terms?)</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>reroute logic into <b>Deal Workspace</b> · <b>Discovery Studio</b> · <b>Pilot Desk</b></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>Failure-pattern diagnosis</li><li>Consequential route correction</li><li>Strategic severity</li><li>The pinned-as-evidence posture (count dynamic, never hardcoded)</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Always connect risk review to specific evidence and corrective action</li><li>Not a status dashboard</li><li>Not a boxed warning-board</li><li>Not abstract diagnosis without a corrective move</li></ul></div></div></div>
