 <div class="map"><h2>4. What this room is for and how it works</h2><p>The room's capability map: its purpose, every part and what it does, what flows in from and out to other rooms, and what it must never become.</p><div class="wrap">
-  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Prospecting Desk · Decision Bench · capability map</div><h1>Find accounts, confirm each one, send only the real ones on.</h1><div class="fam">Decision Bench (strategic shaping) · renamed from Sourcing Workbench 2026-07-03 · settled 2026-07-04</div><p>Find accounts, confirm each one is real and worth it, and send only the confirmed ones to Signal Console. Keep the funnel moving — never a filing cabinet. <b>Antaeus runs its own web research</b>: the operator describes who they want in plain language, and Antaeus reads public news, funding announcements, job posts and company pages, and brings back companies that match — each cited with a link.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.6 (the search mind-correction, 2026-07-03) + shipped src/sourcing-workbench. Settled design: prospecting-desk-funnel-2026-07-04.html (variant F1: Find → Confirm → Send).</div></div>
-  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Run one top-to-bottom funnel — <b>Find → Confirm → Send</b>. The room does not plug into Sales Navigator or buy contact lists; it runs its own cited web research. Confirm is a real, visible step — the discipline that guards Signal Console. Nothing crosses without it.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The funnel</div><h2>Find → Confirm → Send</h2><table><tr><th style="width:150px">Stage</th><th>What happens</th></tr><tr><td><b>Find</b></td><td>the operator describes who they want → Antaeus runs its own web research → cited companies land in “Just added.”</td></tr><tr><td><b>Confirm</b></td><td>three plain questions turn a raw company into a qualified account — the guard on Signal Console</td></tr><tr><td><b>Send</b></td><td>confirmed accounts cross to Signal Console; a ready account can also go to Outbound (first message). Each sends individually.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · The three confirm questions</div><h2>The real, visible confirm step</h2><div class="sd">Plain-language, spoon-fed — nothing insider.</div><ul class="plain"><li><b>Are they who we’re targeting?</b> (does the account fit the focus)</li><li><b>What’s our way in to the account?</b> (the entry point)</li><li><b>How will we reach out?</b> (the approach)</li></ul></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The describe-a-search box</b></td><td>Plain-language ask → Antaeus web research, each result cited.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Saved searches + auto-watches</b></td><td>run-on-demand searches the operator triggers + watches Antaeus re-runs on its own and alerts on — with a productivity read + a dry-search flag.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Add-returned-company</b></td><td>Pull a cited company into the funnel.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Quality score + what’s-missing</b></td><td>How complete an account is + what still needs answering.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The three-question confirm</b></td><td>The guard step (above).</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Who-to-target guidance</b></td><td>Rides the active focus — “go for the VP of RevOps who owns the forecast, not the junior rep who fills the CRM.”</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The stage lifecycle</b></td><td>just added → confirmed → ready → sent, + set-aside-with-reason; counts per stage.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li><b>Territory Architect</b> — focus/division, tier, approach vocabulary + who-to-target</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>confirmed accounts → <b>Signal Console</b></li><li>a ready account → <b>Outbound Studio</b> (first message)</li><li>carries focus + approach context forward</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>The honesty of the search — Antaeus runs its OWN web research, cited (never claim a vendor/Sales-Nav feed it doesn’t have)</li><li>Confirm as a real step (accounts pass the three questions before Signal Console)</li><li>Who-to-target guidance</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never a filing cabinet</li><li>Never a “pretend search”</li><li>Not a Sales Navigator integration</li><li>Not a bought-list importer</li></ul></div></div></div>
+<div class="callout blue"><div class="ct">Language and capability review · 2026-11-02</div><div class="cb">Use the current source and docs/language-remediation-2026 for implementation. Earlier design references below preserve history; they do not authorize deprecated customer language or capabilities that the source does not implement. Keep stable internal identifiers separate from display wording. Distinguish evidence, assessment, forecast, and recommendation.</div></div>
