 <div class="map"><h2>4. What this room is for and how it works</h2><p>The room's capability map: its purpose, every part and what it does, what flows in from and out to other rooms, and what it must never become.</p><div class="wrap">
-  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Quota Workback · System Ledger · capability map</div><h1>The annual number, worked down to what you do every day.</h1><div class="fam">System Ledger (synthesis) · design settled 2026-07-07 (pace + fused strands)</div><p>Turn a quota target into execution pressure the seller can <b>feel</b> — the annual number worked all the way down to the one thing they control: what they do every working day. Quota math is execution pressure, not isolated planning.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.18 + the calc() + computeCoverage engine (shipped src/quota-workback). Settled design: quota-workback-pace-strands-2026-07-07.html.</div></div>
-  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Working backward from the number, answer three things and nothing else: the <b>daily habit</b> the number demands, whether the <b>plan is even real</b>, and whether there’s <b>enough in flight</b>. The daily number is the one dominant state; believability + coverage support it; the funnel arithmetic recedes.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The three answers</div><h2>What the room resolves</h2><table><tr><th style="width:26px">#</th><th style="width:200px">Answer</th><th>What it shows</th></tr><tr><td><span class="n">1</span></td><td><b>The daily habit</b></td><td>the outreach/day, meetings/week, real opportunities & deals/quarter the number actually demands</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">2</span></td><td><b>Is the plan even real</b></td><td>a believability check against the benchmark for your deal size — calling out the ONE optimistic assumption + what it costs if you’re wrong (the room’s soul)</td></tr><tr><td><span class="n">3</span></td><td><b>Enough in flight</b></td><td>live pipeline coverage pulled from Deal Workspace — the gap in real dollars</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · The two reads</div><h2>Plan (setting) vs Pace (returning)</h2><div class="sd">The room ships in two reads over the same math.</div><table><tr><th style="width:150px">Read</th><th>For</th><th>Dominant surface</th></tr><tr><td><b>Plan</b></td><td>setting the number — works on an empty workspace</td><td>the derived daily habit</td></tr><tr><td><b>Pace</b></td><td>a returning seller</td><td>projected year-end landing vs target · what-the-number-needs vs where-you-actually-are · the move back on pace</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The annual number (quota)</b></td><td>The target the whole room works backward from.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Typical deal size (ACV → benchmark band)</b></td><td>SMB / Mid-Market / Enterprise / Strategic — sets which benchmark the believability read tests against.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Win rate + cycle length</b></td><td>The conversion + timing inputs.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The conversion assumptions</b></td><td>Advanced / gated — the funnel arithmetic, recessive.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The derived daily habit</b></td><td>messages & calls a day · first meetings a week · real opportunities & deals a quarter.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The believability read</b></td><td>“this plan is a stretch — one assumption is optimistic” + what it costs. A plain judgment, never a bare score.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Pipeline coverage</b></td><td>From Deal Workspace — ratio vs the band target, weighted vs raw, the dollar gap.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The pace projection</b></td><td>Projected year-end landing vs target + the need-vs-actual scoreboard for a returning seller.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>pipeline from <b>Deal Workspace</b> (coverage)</li><li>logged motion from <b>Outbound</b> / <b>Cold Call</b> (the pace/actuals read)</li><li>onboarding targets</li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>targets into the <b>Dashboard</b></li><li>coverage truth into <b>Readiness</b></li><li>execution pressure (the daily habit) into <b>Outbound</b> + <b>Cold Call</b></li><li>the daily/weekly cadence into <b>Founding GTM</b> §7 (day-one operating rhythm)</li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">6 · Language + open rename</div><h2>Plain, no funnel jargon</h2><div class="sd">Th