 <div class="map"><h2>4. What this room is for and how it works</h2><p>The room's capability map: its purpose, every part and what it does, what flows in from and out to other rooms, and what it must never become.</p><div class="wrap">
-  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Signal Console · Live Instrument · capability map</div><h1>The accounts you’re watching, the signals stacking up, the next move on each.</h1><div class="fam">Live Instrument (live execution) · protected room · settled 2026-07-04 (Attention Router)</div><p>The room where the operator tracks the named accounts they’re watching, the signals attached to each, and the next move on each. Accounts come in by hand or from enrichment; signals stack up against them; the operator decides what to act on. Signals are <b>time-limited events</b> — research on a qualified account may justify motion, but research without motion is collection theater.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.7 + the heat engine (shipped src/signal-console) + ADR-006 (substrate role). Settled design: signal-console-attention-router-2026-07-04.html.</div></div>
-  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Rank the watched field by <b>where attention should go</b>. Account heat feeds Dashboard command ranking. Post-ADR-006 the room is also the <b>data substrate</b> the Briefing reads from — accounts + signals live in the <span class="mono">signal_console_accounts</span> + <span class="mono">signals</span> Postgres tables this room owns. The Briefing reads; it never writes back.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The heat engine</div><h2>How an account ranks</h2><div class="sd">Heat is computed, not stored — the source of truth is the signals + their timestamps.</div><ul class="plain"><li><b>Heat = signal count × type weight × source credibility × recency decay</b></li><li>Bands (the Attention Router): <b>act now</b> · <b>reach while warm</b> · <b>emerging</b> · <b>going cold</b> — the relevance is felt as a band, not a bare number</li></ul></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The account list</b></td><td>The named accounts being watched — sorted by where attention should go.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Signal records</b></td><td>Time-limited events attached to each account.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Heat score per account</b></td><td>The computed rank (above) — feeds Dashboard command ranking.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The morning brief</b></td><td>The daily read on the watched field.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Research posture</b></td><td>“motion ready” vs “research heavy” — guards against collection theater.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The workspace-health block</b></td><td>compounding vs still weak.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The enrich-all flow</b></td><td>Pull enrichment (triggers / firmographics / heat) across the field.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Add-account</b></td><td>By hand or from Prospecting Desk enrichment.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>accounts from <b>Prospecting Desk</b> + <b>Territory Architect</b></li><li>ICP-Match score from <b>ICP Studio</b></li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>ranked accounts → <b>Outbound Studio</b> · <b>Cold Call Studio</b> · <b>LinkedIn Playbook</b></li><li>heat + readiness → <b>Dashboard</b></li><li>heat + motion state → <b>Handoff Kit</b></li><li>accounts + signals → the <b>Briefing</b> (read-only substrate per ADR-006)</li><li>act-on handoffs → <b>Outbound</b> · <b>Discovery Studio</b> · <b>Cold Call</b> · <b>Deal Workspace</b></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>Signal interpretation</li><li>Account-to-motion logic (research without motion is collection theater)</li><li>Account priority meaning</li><li>A protected room — may not be made generic, renamed, or folded in</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never a badge list</li><li>Never a passive timeline</li><li>Not a notification feed</li><li>Not a static account directory</li></ul></div></div></div>
+<div class="callout blue"><div class="ct">Language and capability review · 2026-11-02</div><div class="cb">Use the current source and docs/language-remediation-2026 for implementation. Earlier design references below preserve history; they do not authorize deprecated customer language or capabilities that the source does not implement. Keep stable internal identifiers separate from display wording. Distinguish evidence, assessment, forecast, and recommendation.</div></div>
+  <div class="mast"><div class="k">Signal Console · execution workflow · capability map</div><h1>Monitor account signals and priority.</h1><div class="fam">execution workflow (live execution) · protected room · settled 2026-07-04 (Attention Router)</div><p>Signal Console stores watched accounts and supporting signals, then ranks them using signal type, credibility, and age. Review those inputs before recommending outreach.</p><div class="src">Sourced from: canon §4.7 + the heat engine (shipped src/signal-console) + ADR-006 (substrate role). Settled design: signal-console-attention-router-2026-07-04.html.</div></div>
+  <div class="sec"><div class="sn">1 · Purpose</div><h2>What the room is for</h2><div class="sd">Explain account priority using current signals and recorded activity. Preserve the ranking math and data contracts. Research is useful when it supports a specific account decision; do not infer buyer intent or urgency merely from a score.</div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">2 · The account-priority engine</div><h2>How an account ranks</h2><div class="sd">Priority is computed, not stored — the source of truth is the signals + their timestamps.</div><ul class="plain"><li><b>Priority score = signal count × type weight × source credibility × recency decay</b></li><li>Bands (the Attention Router): <b>act now</b> · <b>reach while warm</b> · <b>emerging</b> · <b>going cold</b> — the relevance is felt as a band, not a bare number</li></ul></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">3 · What it offers</div><h2>The primitives</h2><table><tr><th style="width:230px">Capability / surface</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The account list</b></td><td>The named accounts being watched — sorted by where attention should go.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Signal records</b></td><td>Time-limited events attached to each account.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Priority score per account</b></td><td>The computed rank (above) — feeds Dashboard command ranking.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The morning brief</b></td><td>A daily summary of watched-account signals.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Research posture</b></td><td>Distinguish accounts with enough context for outreach from accounts that still need research.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The workspace-health block</b></td><td>compounding vs still weak.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>The enrich-all flow</b></td><td>Refresh signals, firmographics, and account-priority inputs for watched accounts.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:230px"><b>Add-account</b></td><td>By hand or from Prospecting Desk enrichment.</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">4 · Flows</div><h2>What comes in, what goes out</h2><div class="flows"><div class="flowcol inn"><div class="fh">Flows in</div><ul class="plain"><li>accounts from <b>Prospecting Desk</b> + <b>Territory Architect</b></li><li>ICP-Match score from <b>ICP Studio</b></li></ul></div><div class="flowcol out"><div class="fh">Flows out</div><ul class="plain"><li>ranked accounts → <b>Outbound Studio</b> · <b>Cold Call Studio</b> · <b>LinkedIn Playbook</b></li><li>account priority + available evidence → <b>Dashboard</b></li><li>account priority + activity state → <b>sales handoff documentation</b></li><li>accounts + signals → the <b>Briefing</b> (read-only substrate per ADR-006)</li><li>act-on handoffs → <b>Outbound</b> · <b>Discovery Studio</b> · <b>Cold Call</b> · <b>Deal Workspace</b></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="sec"><div class="sn">5 · Guardrails</div><h2>Must never be flattened · what it is NOT</h2><div class="two"><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--red)">Must never be flattened</div><ul class="plain"><li>Signal interpretation</li><li>Connect account research to a concrete outreach or monitoring decision</li><li>Account priority meaning</li><li>A protected room — may not be made generic, renamed, or folded in</li></ul></div><div><div class="sn" style="color:var(--ink-3)">What it is NOT</div><ul class="plain"><li>Never a badge list</li><li>Never a passive timeline</li><li>Not a notification feed</li><li>Not a static account directory</li></ul></div></div></div>
